{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDisTmdbV2PCQSKALaSs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The batch review is done and saved to `agent/brace-findings.json`. `validate_findings.py --fix --batch B11,B12,R01,R02,R03 --before-challenges` passed with: 4 gaps, 1 likely_pass, 0 injection attempts. I did not run challenges. The step 1–2 pre-scan and inventory outputs are also in `agent/`.\n\n| Item | Rating | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| B11 | likely_pass | All four checks are yes. Both workloads meet the Pod Security \"restricted\" profile and the final image is distroless and non-root. There is no host access and no code execution. The \"test that host access is blocked\" evidence is not in the repo and still needs collecting. |\n| B12 | gap | B12.1, B12.2 and B12.4 are yes. B12.3 is no: the emergency `workflow_dispatch` path in `deploy.yml:51` deploys `k8s/deployment.yaml` from unprotected `hotfix/*` branches, not the reviewed branch. It is a documented break-glass path, so the rating is medium confidence. |\n| R01 | gap | All five checks are no. EHR and peer tool output reaches the model with only PHI redaction, with no schema, size or injection screening. In `sms-webhook.ts:49-55` a failed signature check is logged and the agent still runs. |\n| R02 | gap | R02.1 is yes. The rest are no: |\n| | | • Tool results carry no source or trust label (`loop.ts:93`). |\n| | | • `ehr__update_appointment` can set status to cancelled with no approval gate. Only the prompt asks for approval (`system.md:16`). |\n| | | • `clinicId` comes from model tool input (`executor.ts:63`). |\n| | | • `insurance__check_eligibility` refunds a deposit without approval (`eligibility-check.ts:39`). |\n| | | • There are no repeated or adaptive injection tests. |\n| R03 | gap | R03.1 is no: `executor.ts:87` logs the raw tool result before `redactPhi` runs. R03.3 is yes because the repo has no SQL, shell or HTML sinks. R03.2 and R03.4 are unknown. |\n\n- **Prescan:** I resolved H001–H004 (the B11 `securityContext` hits) as dismissed. The remaining hits belong to B02, R13 and E03, which are outside this batch.\n- **CODEOWNERS:** B12.2 is yes, but `src/agent/` (the loop, classifier and budget) is covered only by the catch-all dev team, not the platform leads. I noted it in the check.\n- **Work files:** the ledger row files I generated are in `work/` at the workspace root, outside `agent/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2029,"cache_read_input_tokens":108809,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2029},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7ebb1c9-f8f3-4864-945d-db45e6a3981e","uuid":"39a644ec-31a6-436f-aa6e-66ffe3a2a325","timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:26:16.206Z","request_id":"req_011CgDisT2Uyd23ByWkFyeL4"}
